    "remaining_guide": {
      "path": "porting/rust-parity-plan-20261026/REMAINING-WORK.md",
      "git_blob": "008d934cde44f93ebf0dc9028ff52fb29265c204",
      "sha256": "6a9b9799db24f8641f3b930622396b168f3fff124adaf0bd820d725548c0242f",
      "lines": 148,
      "verified_anchors": [
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "SysON feature parity is still open. Rust foundations and several repairs are on main, but the connected application, complete language and semantic behavior, usable views, durable storage and release qualification still need work. Our next product milestone is a project that a user can create or import, edit, save, reload, reopen and inspect after a backend restart without manually reimporting JSON."
        },
        {
          "line": 71,
          "text": "## Deliver the first durable Rust workflow"
        },
        {
          "line": 81,
          "text": "Keep the batch13 long-name counterexample: `Long <&> \u96ea\ud83e\udded ` + 4096 `x` characters + ` END` (4,113 UTF-16 units; 4,117 UTF-8 bytes). Native SysON retained it after save/reselect/page reload; Rust required explicit reimport. The 4,442-byte Rust export/reimport remains bounded evidence. Page reload and backend restart are separate gates, and the native artifact's source gap still limits parity claims."
        }
      ]
    },
